cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "TDR Painter: an in-browser TDR and S-parameter teaching tool"
message: >-
  If you use TDR Painter in teaching, a talk or a publication, please cite it
  using the metadata in this file.
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Maghlakelidze
    given-names: Giorgi
    email: giorgi.m@ieee.org
    affiliation: Missouri University of Science and Technology
    orcid: https://orcid.org/0000-0003-1865-4996
repository-code: "https://github.com/Sparamix/tdr-painter"
url: "https://sparamix.github.io/tdr-painter/"
abstract: >-
  TDR Painter is a single-page, offline teaching tool for signal and power
  integrity. The user paints a time-domain reflectometry (TDR) impedance
  profile, drops in lumped and distributed elements (shunt C, series L and R,
  open and shorted stubs, resistive pads), and sees S11, S21, insertion-loss
  deviation, the power balance and the TDR update live. The model is an
  ABCD cascade of lossy TEM line cells with a Djordjevic-Sarkar dielectric and
  a skin-effect conductor model. It is verified against independent scikit-rf
  models, textbook closed forms and two published scikit-rf cases (a VNA
  measurement and an ANSYS Circuit simulation).
keywords:
  - signal integrity
  - power integrity
  - time-domain reflectometry
  - TDR
  - S-parameters
  - impedance profile
  - transmission lines
  - engineering education
